{{/* @dot github.com/donseba/go-partial/examples/docs.DocsPage */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400 text-[13px] font-extrabold uppercase text-emerald-300">exp</p>
    <h1 class="max-w-4xl text-5xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-slate-50">Flash messages</h1>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/flash</code> renders request-scoped messages for SSR and HTMX responses. It stays deliberately small: your app owns persistence, while the package owns message shape, helpers, and default markup.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Register helpers</h2>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root.SetFunc(flash.FuncMap())
root.Use(flash.Stage())</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Add messages</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Flash messages live on context. In handlers, start from <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">r.Context()</code>, add messages, then render with the derived request context.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">ctx := flash.Add(r.Context(),
    flash.Success("Saved"),
    flash.Info("Profile refreshed"),
    flash.Warn("Using cached data"),
    flash.Error("Payment failed"),
)

r = r.WithContext(ctx)
page := root.Clone()
_ = partial.Write(ctx, w, r, page)</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Render in templates</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Use <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ flashTarget }}" }}</code> once in the page shell when HTMX fragments should append messages to a stable place. Use <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ flash }}" }}</code> where the current request should render its messages.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">{{ "{{ flash }}" }}

{{ "{{ if hasFlashes }}" }}
    {{ "{{ range flashes }}" }}{{ "{{ .Level }}" }}: {{ "{{ .Text }}" }}{{ "{{ end }}" }}
{{ "{{ end }}" }}</code></pre>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;body&gt;
    {{ "{{ content }}" }}
    {{ "{{ flashTarget }}" }}
&lt;/body&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Override markup</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The default message and target templates are embedded. Applications can replace either one with templates from their own filesystem or fully configured partials.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root.Use(flash.Stage(
    flash.WithTemplate("templates/flash.gohtml"),
    flash.WithTargetTemplate("templates/flash target.gohtml"),
    flash.WithTargetID("flash-messages"),
))</code></pre>

    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Templates receive <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">flash.Data</code> with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Messages []flash.Message</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">TargetID</code>. Built-in levels are <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">success</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">info</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">warn</code>, and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">error</code>. Custom levels and target IDs are normalized into lowercase CSS-friendly tokens so templates can safely use them in classes, attributes, and OOB selectors.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Across a redirect</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Persist</code> of a <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">flash.Cookie</code> keeps messages for the next request in a cookie, with their level; <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Restore</code> moves them into that request's store and clears the cookie, so <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ flash }}" }}</code> shows them once.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">cookie := flash.Cookie{Key: key}

cookie.Persist(w, flash.Success("Saved"))
http.Redirect(w, r, "/items", http.StatusSeeOther)

// For every request, such as in middleware:
r = cookie.Restore(w, r)</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The fields of <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">flash.Cookie</code> set the cookie's name, path, lifetime and size; with a <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Key</code> it is signed, so only messages the application persisted are shown.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Browser client</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The browser client, served from <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">clients.FS()</code>, is a small script that hides messages after a time per level (success and info 5s, warn 8s, error never; change it with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-flash-autohide-&lt;level&gt;</code> or <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-flash-autohide</code>), keeps a message under the pointer or focus, removes it when a <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-flash-dismiss</code> element in it is clicked and dispatches <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial:flash</code> for each message. With <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-flash-request-error</code> on the flash target, failed requests of htmx, Unpoly and Turbo show that text as an error.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">mux.Handle("GET /assets/", http.StripPrefix("/assets/", http.FileServerFS(clients.FS())))</code></pre>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;script src="/assets/partial-flash.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;div id="flash-messages" class="partial-flash-target" data-flash-request-error="Something went wrong"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Client templates and request errors</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ flashTemplate }}" }}</code> renders the flash template of the stage as a <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">&lt;template data-flash-template="error"&gt;</code> per level, which the browser client clones for the messages it shows itself, so they look like those of the server. More attributes on the flash target: <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-flash-request-error-replace</code> keeps one request error at a time, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-flash-request-error-body</code> shows the text/plain sentence of a refused request (4xx) without htmx swapping it, and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-flash-request-error-skip-flash</code> adds nothing to a failed response that brings its own message. Escape dismisses the message that has the focus.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;div id="flash-messages" data-flash-request-error="The request failed."
     data-flash-request-error-replace data-flash-request-error-body data-flash-request-error-skip-flash&gt;
    {{ "{{ flashTemplate }}" }}
    {{ "{{ flash }}" }}
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">flash.WithRequestErrors(flash.RequestErrors{Text, Replace, Body, SkipFlash})</code> makes the stage write these attributes itself, in <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ flashTarget }}" }}</code> and in <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ flashTargetAttrs }}" }}</code>, which also writes the target's id and takes a text of the template's own, such as a translated one. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ flashTemplate }}" }}</code> writes nothing in a partial rendered out of band. A response with an error status that htmx swaps, such as a 422 form re-render with htmx 4, is no failed request: with htmx 4 the client decides at <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">htmx:finally:request</code>.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Refusing a request</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">flash.Respond</code> answers a refused request with messages: out of band in the flash target, with the template of the parent's flash stage, leaving the target as it is (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Reswap: none</code>), or as text/plain for a request of no client library. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">flash.RenderOOB(ctx, messages...)</code> renders the same from a render stage; <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">ext/errors</code> uses it with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">WithFlash(fn)</code>.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">if !allowed {
    _ = flash.Respond(w, r, root, http.StatusForbidden, flash.Error("You may not do this."))
    return
}</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The clients are files of <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">clients.FS()</code>, with the clients of <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/sse</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/interactions</code>, for applications that fingerprint their assets.</p>
</article>

